{
 "version": 1,
 "_notes": "Method: for each study the labels.u8.gz volume was read with Node zlib and, per organ group (lung, liver, spleen, kidney, stomach, pancreas, adrenal, gallbladder, heart, bladder, prostate, hip, sacrum, gluteus maximus), the 1st/99th percentile slice of the voxel-count histogram along z (axis 2, RAS: higher index is more superior in every study) was taken as its bottom/top, skipping extents cut off by the volume edge. Trunk frac: 0 = lung apex, 0.45 = liver dome (diaphragm), 0.8 = iliac crest (top of hip bone), 1.0 = ischial tuberosity (bottom of hip bone). The six TotalSegmentator CTs with an apex or pelvis in view were anchored directly (piecewise linear 'anchors', [frac, slice] pairs); a reference frac per organ extent was the median over those CTs; every other trunk study was fitted by least squares of slice against that reference (rms residual in 'fit'). Head frac: 0 = vertex, 1 = foramen magnum. 'frac' and 'slices' are the span the study covers after clipping to 0..1 and to the volume; 'anchors' (when present) maps frac to slice piecewise and extrapolates nowhere. windowAt switches a CT to the lung window where the slice is between lung apex and diaphragm (frac 0.03-0.38); 'dims' is the voxel count along the axis. Entries marked approx are small crops placed by their organ position. Keys with @suffix reuse the study in 'studyId'. Limb entries (ts-mr-s0056) are the left knee: femur = thigh, tibia = leg; 'side' is the anatomical side of the segment. Regenerate by re-running the same measurement; do not hand-edit slices. Visible Human CTs (vh-*): proximal is the high slice in all four (RAS). Forearm: elbow end = volume top z104, wrist z42 (class 201 bone extent). Thigh and leg fractions assume femur 450 mm and tibia 380 mm; thigh position set from the femoral isthmus. Head: vertex z123 to foramen magnum z51; neck: z51 to z0. Ultrasound fracSpan for these studies maps the WHOLE volume (study frac = 1 - (frac - a)/(b - a)), so a and b can lie outside 0..1.",
